body:
**Found:** 2026-10-20, moving a host's report checks from reading `TestRunReport.json` to `kronikol query`, as 5.0.0's compressed data file asks. Its tests check what its own capture became: a scenario looked up by the test id it recorded, that scenario's calls by caller and service, and the PlantUML of all its diagrams. Each needed a workaround through the engine.

**Versions:** 5.0.0, the latest. Line references are to `f2f7179` (v5.0.0).

---

## What happens

- **No test id.** A `scenarios --json` item has `address`, `stableId`, `feature`, `scenario` and the rest, but not the scenario's `id` ([`QueryCommand.Overview.cs` L264-L281](https://github.com/lemonlion/Kronikol/blob/f2f717903c486b48826de032a2b3a8381a414d04/src/Kronikol/Query/QueryCommand.Overview.cs#L264-L281)). A host knows each test by the id it wrote into the tests file, so it has to match on the name, and the name it gets back is not the one it wrote: `CapitaliseTitles` turned `lists orders` into `Lists orders`.
- **No diagram count, and one diagram per call.** Nothing says how many diagrams a scenario has, and `diagram` takes one `sN/dK` and writes only to `--out` ([`QueryCommand.Payloads.cs` L633-L654](https://github.com/lemonlion/Kronikol/blob/f2f717903c486b48826de032a2b3a8381a414d04/src/Kronikol/Query/QueryCommand.Payloads.cs#L633-L654)). Reading all of a scenario's diagrams is a call per diagram and then one that fails, `No diagram d1 in s0 — it has 1.` at exit 2, which a script has to tell apart from a real usage error by its text. For a script driving `query.cs` that is a process per diagram: about 200 for a 100-scenario run.
- **No caller.** An `interactions --json` item has `service` but not the caller ([`QueryCommand.Payloads.cs` L127-L143](https://github.com/lemonlion/Kronikol/blob/f2f717903c486b48826de032a2b3a8381a414d04/src/Kronikol/Query/QueryCommand.Payloads.cs#L127-L143)), though `callerName` is in the data file. It is what tells a user's action from the calls it caused, or one client's calls from another's.

One test, written as `lists orders` with id `0af7651916cd43dd8448eb211c80319c`, making one call from `orders-ui` to `orders-api`:

```
$ query scenarios --json   (exit 0)
{… "items":[{"address":"s0","stableId":"098687d2835c47eb","feature":"Orders","scenario":"Lists orders","result":"Passed","failed":false,"durationSeconds":1,"interactions":2,"errorMessage":null,"attempt":null,"stableIdShared":1,"tags":[],"exampleValues":{}}], …}

$ query interactions s0 --json   (exit 0)
{… "items":[{"address":"s0/i0","scenario":"s0","service":"orders-api","method":"GET","uri":"http://orders-api/orders","summary":"GET /orders","status":"OK","statusCode":null,"durationMs":10,"stepPath":null,"request":{"bodyHash":null,"bodyLength":0},"response":{"bodyHash":"b:97d170e1","bodyLength":2}}], …}

$ query diagram s0/d1 --out d1.puml   (exit 2)
[stderr] No diagram d1 in s0 — it has 1.
```

<details><summary>The repro: <code>dotnet run --file query-gaps.cs -- &lt;empty folder&gt;</code>, which shows this and two related gaps</summary>

```csharp
#:package Kronikol@5.0.0
#:property PublishAot=false
// One test that makes one call carrying a header, and two taps that each report a degraded capture. Then the questions a
// host asks of the report through the query engine, now that the data file is compressed.
using Kronikol.Ingestion;
using Kronikol.Query;
using Kronikol.Reports;

Environment.SetEnvironmentVariable("KRONIKOL_HISTORY", "off");
var dir = args[0];
var tests = Path.Combine(dir, "tests.ndjson");
var calls = Path.Combine(dir, "calls.ndjson");
File.WriteAllLines(tests,
[
    """{"event":"start","testId":"0af7651916cd43dd8448eb211c80319c","testName":"lists orders","feature":"Orders","timestamp":"2026-01-01T10:00:00.000Z"}""",
    """{"event":"end","testId":"0af7651916cd43dd8448eb211c80319c","status":"passed","durationMs":1000,"timestamp":"2026-01-01T10:00:01.000Z"}""",
]);
File.WriteAllLines(calls,
[
    """{"type":"Request","testId":"0af7651916cd43dd8448eb211c80319c","testName":"lists orders","requestResponseId":"a","method":"GET","uri":"http://orders-api/orders","serviceName":"orders-api","callerName":"orders-ui","headers":[{"key":"x-debug-token","value":"needle-in-a-header"}],"timestamp":"2026-01-01T10:00:00.500Z"}""",
    """{"type":"Response","testId":"0af7651916cd43dd8448eb211c80319c","testName":"lists orders","requestResponseId":"a","method":"GET","uri":"http://orders-api/orders","serviceName":"orders-api","callerName":"orders-ui","statusCode":"OK","content":"[]","timestamp":"2026-01-01T10:00:00.510Z"}""",
]);

var options = IngestPipeline.DefaultOptions();
options.ReportsFolderPath = Path.Combine(dir, "out");
IngestPipeline.Run(new IngestRequest
{
    InteractionFiles = [calls],
    TestsFile = tests,
    Options = options,
    HostDiagnostics =
    [
        new DiagnosticEntry(DiagnosticKind.CaptureDegraded, "tap-a: 3 oversize payload(s) streamed past"),
        new DiagnosticEntry(DiagnosticKind.CaptureDegraded, "tap-b: decoding disabled on 1 connection(s)"),
    ],
});

void Ask(params string[] command)
{
    using var output = new StringWriter();
    using var error = new StringWriter();
    var exit = QueryCommand.Run([command[0], options.ReportsFolderPath, .. command[1..]], output, error);
    Console.WriteLine($"$ query {string.Join(' ', command)}   (exit {exit})");
    Console.WriteLine(output.ToString().TrimEnd());
    if (error.ToString().Trim() is { Length: > 0 } said)
        Console.WriteLine($"[stderr] {said}");
    Console.WriteLine();
}

Ask("grep", "needle-in-a-header", "--count");
Ask("grep", "needle-in-a-header", "--in", "bodies,uris,steps,assertions,names,errors,headers,notes", "--count");
Ask("grep", "needle-in-a-header");
Ask("summary", "--json");
Ask("scenarios", "--json");
Ask("interactions", "s0", "--json");
Ask("diagram", "s0/d1", "--out", Path.Combine(dir, "d1.puml"));
```

`PublishAot=false` because a file-based app turns reflection-based JSON off by default, which `InteractionRecord.FromJson` needs.

</details>

## Suggestion

- `id` and `diagrams` (how many) on each `scenarios --json` item, and perhaps an `id:<testId>` address beside `sid:`.
- `caller` on each `interactions --json` item.
- `diagram sN --out DIR`: every diagram of the scenario, `sN-d0.puml` onwards, in one call.

Related: #182 and #183 (found in the same move).
